<title>POLAND: KPW CLEARS NOVITA ISSUE OF 1.1 MLN SHRS.</title>
<headline>KPW CLEARS NOVITA ISSUE OF 1.1 MLN SHRS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission (KPW) has cleared for public trade 1,116,000 shares in carpet maker Novita SA for its convertible bond issue, the KPW said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Each bond, carrying a nine-percent coupon, is exchangeable into 4,916 shares.</p>
<p>In June the firm set the conversion price for the bonds at 20.3 zlotys and said it had offered 227 of them to selected investors.</p>
<p>Investors can order the bonds converted by May 31, 2000, two months before the bonds would be redeemed at 120 percent of their par value.</p>
<p>Novita closed on Thursday at 18.3 zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
